Comment:
 Plaid Pi is an image for the Orange Pi 5B built from Ubuntu 26.04 packages with the
 Armbian build framework and Armbian's Rockchip vendor kernel. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by Canonical, Armbian, Rockchip, Arm, Google, Mozilla, Microsoft or Shenzhen Xunlong.
 .
 What Plaid Pi adds to the image, and the licence of each part:
 .
  * Plaid Pi's own programs and scripts (/usr/local/bin/pidesktop-*, /usr/local/sbin/pidesktop-*,
    the two Files add-ons, the Network Drive window and its root helper, systemd units, configuration):
    GPL-3.0-or-later.
  * Plaid Pi's artwork (the Plaid wallpaper, the penguin screensaver clip and still, the tartan
    terminal logo, the pi-desktop logo and the installer icons): CC BY-SA 4.0.
  * Kernel: Armbian's linux-rockchip branch rk-6.1-rkr7.2 at commit 44bbd021d7808cab93d1f2d64c1f092038257576,
    merged with upstream stable Linux 6.1.189, with the Plaid Pi patches (GPL-2.0). Complete source:
    https://github.com/defcom5-rockchip/linux-rockchip tag pi-desktop-5.0, and the patches in the recipe
    repository (userpatches/kernel/).
  * Boot loader: Armbian's build of radxa/u-boot branch next-dev-v2024.10 commit 39cd993e5d6296635438e84f4576b3a9bf76f86e,
    unmodified (GPL-2.0+), with Rockchip's binary boot blobs (rkbin, Rockchip's licence).
  * Packages Plaid Pi rebuilt or patched (sources in the recipe repository): gnome-control-center (+pd3),
    Rhythmbox 3.5.1, PipeWire 1.6.10 / WirePlumber 0.5.18 (upstream PipeWire 1.6.10 on Debian's 1.6.9-2
    packaging, Debian's WirePlumber 0.5.18-1, rebuilt as ~pd55), rockchip-vaapi 3.5.0 (https://github.com/defcom5-rockchip/rockchip-vaapi),
    librockchip-mpp +pd34 (eight Plaid Pi patches: AV1 deferred refresh, and the VP9 frame-label wrap of
    rockchip-linux/mpp PR #976; Apache-2.0), librga (rebuilt for 26.04), the libmali-hook shim, gst-plugins-good
    (+pd1, one upstream FLAC fix), and mpv (Ubuntu's mpv 0.41.0-2ubuntu4 rebuilt with two patches and Plaid Pi's
    mpv.conf as +pd2; GPL-3.0+ as linked). Complete source for mpv, gst-plugins-good, librockchip-mpp, PipeWire and WirePlumber is
    published with each Plaid Pi release next to the image, and the patches and build scripts are in the recipe repository (mpv/, gst-plugins-good/).
  * Pro Updates 1.5.0, the update window (pro-updates, pro-updates-gui and its root helper): GPL-3.0-or-later,
    by the Plaid Pi maintainer. Source: https://github.com/defcom5-rockchip/pro-updates tag v1.5.0; licence
    details in /usr/share/doc/pro-updates/copyright.
  * libpidesktop-ffmali (/usr/local/lib/pidesktop-firefox-mali), the small library Plaid Pi's Firefox launcher loads so
    the unmodified Firefox can use the hardware video decoder with the Mali driver: LGPL-2.1-or-later, Plaid Pi's.
    Complete source in /usr/share/pi-desktop/firefox/. Not part of Firefox; not made or endorsed by Mozilla.
  * The Plaid look: the Dhruva dock (/usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/dhruva@narkagni), Dhruva 3.1 by NarkAgni,
    GPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/narkagni/dhruva commit 95462d4, with one Plaid Pi change (src/core/autohide/EdgeDetection.js, 2026-10-13: the dock's pressure barrier is rebuilt when the monitor geometry changes) (its LICENSE file is installed with it); the Plaid Panel top bar and Killswitch (/usr/local/bin/killswitch), Plaid Pi's, GPL-3.0-or-later; the Plaid
    icon theme (/usr/share/icons/Plaid), Adwaita's folder icons recoloured, CC BY-SA 3.0 US or LGPL-3.0 as Adwaita
    (see its COPYING). Details: /usr/share/pi-desktop/look/README.
  * Arm Mali user-space driver (libmali): Arm's end-user licence, see /usr/share/doc/libmali-*/copyright.
  * Wireless/Bluetooth firmware: Armbian's armbian-firmware package (vendor licences).
 .
 Everything else is unmodified Ubuntu 26.04 (ports.ubuntu.com), Armbian (apt.armbian.com), xtradeb or Ubuntu
 Mozilla Team PPA packages; their sources are in those archives at the versions listed in the release manifest.

